Phase 1
Define the purpose
FUNCTION: what is it supposed to do
INPUT: what feeds into the script
OUTPUT: what output is the script supposed to generate
RULES: Must not contain uppercase letters. Must be 3 to 63 characters long.

Phase 2
Build the blueprint
Writing actual code in this phase is forbidden.
Break the rules down into chronological steps using plain English. If a step feels too big, break it into two.

Phase 3
Translate into code
Look at the comments in English, translate them into Python underneath them then move on.

Phase 4
Once the code works, delete  obvious comments to keep the file clean.
